    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1257">

                <pb facs="1224" n="1058" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1058"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.5034/34</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Thurston, in charge of American interests, to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-08T22:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 8, 1917—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s 604, January 6, 4 p.m. to Parker. Refer Parker’s despatch No. 530 of
                    September 27<anchor n="15" xml:id="d1257-f1"/> and enclosures. Local press
                    published decree December 29 extending time limit in which foreigners desiring
                    to acquire certain properties could renounce citizenship rights until April 15,
                    1917. A translation of this decree leaves in to-morrow’s pouch; also a
                    translation of decree requested by the Department.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
